{"id":"020b0f99-fb8b-4868-9925-4e5dde8daa44","object":"chat.completion","created":1785021700,"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\n  \"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    if not isinstance(case, dict):\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"case must be a dict\\\")\\n    text = case.get('text')\\n    if not isinstance(text, str):\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"text must be string\\\")\\n    passes = case.get('passes')\\n    if not isinstance(passes, list):\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"passes must be list\\\")\\n    for p in passes:\\n        if not isinstance(p, dict):\\n            raise ValueError(\\\"pass must be dict\\\")\\n        if not all(k in p for k in ('name','old','new')):\\n            raise ValueError(\\\"pass missing required fields\\\")\\n    max_rounds = case.get('max_rounds')\\n    if not isinstance(max_rounds, int) or max_rounds <= 0:\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"max_rounds must be positive integer\\\")\\n    apps = []\\n    for _ in range(max_rounds):\\n        changed = False\\n        for p in passes:\\n            old = p['old']\\n            new = p['new']\\n            pos = text.find(old)\\n            if pos != -1:\\n                text = text[:pos] + new + text[pos+len(old):]\\n                changed = True\\n                apps.append(p['name'])\\n        if not changed:\\n            return {\\\"applications\\\": apps, \\\"fixed_point\\\": True, \\\"text\\\": text}\\n    return {\\\"applications\\\": apps, \\\"fixed_point\\\": False, \\\"text\\\": text}\"\n}","reasoning_content":"We need to implement `solve(case)` that takes a payload object with fields: text (string), passes (list of objects with name, old, new), max_rounds (integer). The task is to simulate a pass scheduler: apply passes in order, each pass does at most one rewrite per sweep (first eligible rewrite), record passes that change the artifact. Repeat sweeps until no change or max_rounds reached. Return a dict with applications (list of pass names in order they changed the artifact), fixed_point (boolean if fixed point reached, i.e., no change in last sweep before reaching max_rounds or after max_rounds? Actually: \"Repeat full sweeps until none changes or the round budget is consumed.\" So after each full sweep, if any pass changed, continue. If no pass changed, it's a fixed point. If max_rounds reached while still changes, then fixed_point=False. Need to return text (the final artifact). Also note that the passes are applied to the text string, each pass replaces occurrences of old with new. \"Each pass performs at most its first eligible rewrite per sweep.\" That means for each pass, find the first occurrence of old in the current text and replace it with new. Only if that replacement changes the text, record the pass name. Then move to next pass. After all passes done, that's one sweep. Then repeat. Also note: \"interestingness_preserved\", \"restart_policy\", \"cache_semantics\" are mentioned but not in payload. Probably just ignore; the output structure only requires applications, fixed_point, text. Ensure to use only payload fields.\n\nThe output schema: {\"applications\": list of strings, \"fixed_point\": bool, \"text\": string}. Must be exactly these keys.\n\nWe must handle invalid cases: raise ValueError. But the given payload seems valid. We'll validate that required fields exist, text is string, passes is list of dicts with name, old, new (strings), max_rounds is int >= 1. If not, raise ValueError.\n\nImplementation: start with text = case['text']. applications = []. For round in range(max_rounds): changed = False. For pass in passes: old, new = pass['old'], pass['new']. Find first occurrence of old in text: pos = text.find(old). If pos >= 0: replace that occurrence with new: text = text[:pos] + new + text[pos+len(old):]; changed = True; applications.append(pass['name']). After each pass, note: only first eligible rewrite per sweep. So we do one replacement per pass per sweep. After all passes, if not changed: fixed_point=True; break. After loop, if loop completed without break, fixed_point=False (because max_rounds reached while changes still happening). Return dict.\n\nEdge case: if max_rounds=0? Payload likely has >=1. We'll handle as no rounds: fixed_point=False? Actually if max_rounds=0, then presumably no sweeps, text unchanged, applications empty, fixed_point? Probably not fixed point because no attempt? But given schema requires fixed_point bool, we must set it. Since no rounds performed, we can't know if further rounds would change; but per instruction: \"Repeat full sweeps until none changes or the round budget is consumed.\" If budget is 0, then immediately stop, no change occurred, so fixed point? Actually no sweeps done, so no change, so it is trivially a fixed point? But definition: fixed point when no change in a sweep. If no sweep, not a fixed point? I'd argue set fixed_point=True because no change happened. But to be safe, we'll follow typical interpretation: if max_rounds <= 0, treat as no sweeps, fixed_point=True. But input likely ensures positive integer.\n\nWe'll implement as described.\n\nNow produce output JSON with key \"implementation\" containing Python source as string.\n\nWe need to escape newlines, backslashes, quotes properly. We'll write the source code as a string and then JSON-encode it.\n\nLet's write the solve function.\n\nWe'll define:\n\ndef solve(case):\n    # validate\n    if not isinstance(case, dict):\n        raise ValueError(\"case must be a dict\")\n    text = case.get('text')\n    if not isinstance(text, str):\n        raise ValueError(\"text must be string\")\n    passes = case.get('passes')\n    if not isinstance(passes, list):\n        raise ValueError(\"passes must be list\")\n    for p in passes:\n        if not isinstance(p, dict):\n            raise ValueError(\"pass must be dict\")\n        if not all(k in p for k in ('name','old','new')):\n            raise ValueError(\"pass missing required fields\")\n    max_rounds = case.get('max_rounds')\n    if not isinstance(max_rounds, int) or max_rounds <= 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"max_rounds must be positive integer\")\n    \n    apps = []\n    for _ in range(max_rounds):\n        changed = False\n        for p in passes:\n            old = p['old']\n            new = p['new']\n            pos = text.find(old)\n            if pos != -1:\n                text = text[:pos] + new + text[pos+len(old):]\n                changed = True\n                apps.append(p['name'])\n        if not changed:\n            # fixed point reached\n            return {\"applications\": apps, \"fixed_point\": True, \"text\": text}\n    # After max_rounds, if still changes, not fixed point\n    return {\"applications\": apps, \"fixed_point\": False, \"text\": text}\n\nCheck: if no changes in first sweep, we return fixed_point=True. If we break early, same. If we exhaust rounds, fixed_point=False.\n\nWe need to ensure we don't mutate input case. We are only reading, not modifying.\n\nNow produce the final answer: a JSON object with key \"implementation\" and value the Python source string escaped.\n\nI'll write the Python source as a multiline string and then use json.dumps in my mind. I'll manually escape.\n\nThe source: \n\ndef solve(case):\n    ...\n\nI'll write it in one line? No, better as a proper string with newlines.\n\nI'll produce the final JSON.\n\nMake sure no backticks. The response must be exactly a JSON object.\n\nLet's construct."},"logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":1314,"completion_tokens":1711,"total_tokens":3025,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":1280},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":1349},"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":1280,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":34},"system_fingerprint":"fp_8b330d02d0_prod0820_fp8_kvcache_20260402"}